                    "message": "Do you have plan on removing this option? AFAICT, this option is intended for internal use only in `rust.bb`. No other Rust recipes use this option.\n\n(It also causes all other sort of reproducibility headache)\n\nFWIW, if you need something as a reference, I updated `caliptra-sw` to use `crate://` SRC_URI here: [meta-aspeed: caliptra-sw: lock all Rust crates versions](https://github.com/khangng-ampere/openbmc/commit/a2912c8944acde746eddc00440f81227e7648c02). I hope that will help you apply to other recipes if you decide to remove this option (see my commit message for how I did it!)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-aspeed/recipes-support/caliptra-sw/caliptra-sw_git.bb",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vince Chang",
                        "email": "vince_chang@aspeedtech.com",
                        "username": "VinceChang6637"
                    },
                    "message": "I originally used CARGO_DISABLE_BITBAKE_VENDORING because it was simpler and avoided maintaining a large crates.inc list.\n\nI agree this is not ideal for reproducibility, so I\u2019ll try to update the recipe to use the standard Yocto cargo crate flow in the next revision.\nIn the next, we plan to move caliptra-auth-manifest-app to cptra-imgtool, and caliptra-sw will be changed to build caliptra-fw.bin instead. Once that restructuring is done, I\u2019ll revisit the crates handling and remove CARGO_DISABLE_BITBAKE_VENDORING if possible."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-aspeed/recipes-support/caliptra-sw/caliptra-sw_git.bb",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vince Chang",
                        "email": "vince_chang@aspeedtech.com",
                        "username": "VinceChang6637"
                    },
                    "message": "@khangng@os.amperecomputing.com After looking into it, switching caliptra-mcu-sw-native to crates-based build requires quite a bit more work than just removing CARGO_DISABLE_BITBAKE_VENDORING.\n\nThere are multiple git dependencies and workspace interactions that need to be handled properly (e.g. adding them into SRC_URI, patching paths, and ensuring Cargo.lock consistency).\n\nGiven the scope, I\u2019d prefer to keep the current approach for now and avoid introducing a large set of changes in this patch."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-aspeed/recipes-support/caliptra-sw/caliptra-sw_git.bb",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "IMHO this actually breaks any source mirrored based builds where the network is sandcastled out with just packages got from do_fetch. This is obviously another downside along with not being able to reproduce builds."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-aspeed/recipes-support/caliptra-sw/caliptra-sw_git.bb",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vince Chang",
                        "email": "vince_chang@aspeedtech.com",
                        "username": "VinceChang6637"
                    },
                    "message": "Refer to https://github.com/openbmc/openbmc/blob/master/meta-phosphor/recipes-phosphor/webui/webui-vue_git.bb#L40\n```\ndo_compile[network] = \"1\"\n```\nMy understanding is that Cargo, like npm, has its own dependency management ecosystem, and in practice we already have similar behavior in projects like webui-vue where network access is required during the build process."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-aspeed/recipes-support/caliptra-sw/caliptra-sw_git.bb",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "The vue stuff is broken and is so partially because it was written before Yocto had good support for npm. There is support for cargo already. Please use it and don\u2019t enable network. \n\nYou should find plenty of recipes already in the openembedded trees that are rust-based. There are even helper tools for preparing the SRC_URI from your cargo lock file or TOML."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-aspeed/recipes-support/caliptra-sw/caliptra-sw_git.bb",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vince Chang",
                        "email": "vince_chang@aspeedtech.com",
                        "username": "VinceChang6637"
                    },
                    "message": "I updated the reference change in caliptra-mcu-sw. Please help review it.\nIf this approach looks better for generating cptra-imgtool, I can also update cptra-imgtool to build from crates instead.\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/openbmc/+/90315/1"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-aspeed/recipes-support/caliptra-sw/caliptra-sw_git.bb",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "I tried it out. it seems to work. Thanks for looking into it. If you can convert the other recipes, I can do an offline build test."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-aspeed/recipes-support/caliptra-sw/caliptra-sw_git.bb",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vince Chang",
                        "email": "vince_chang@aspeedtech.com",
                        "username": "VinceChang6637"
                    },
                    "message": "The new version of cptra-imgtool will include caliptra-auth-manifest-app. Once the new version of cptra-imgtool is ready, I can convert the cptra-imgtool recipes to use crate builds."
                }
            ],
